# Real GPU training image -- NOT built or run in this repo's CI (no GPU in
# a standard GitHub Actions runner or this repo's dev sandbox). Provided so
# the training-side dependencies (CUDA, bitsandbytes for QLoRA) are pinned
# somewhere real, rather than left as a paragraph of prose.
#
# Build on a self-hosted GPU runner or a training job platform that
# provides a GPU, e.g.:
#   docker build -f Dockerfile.gpu -t conv-llm-finetune:gpu .
#   docker run --gpus all -v $(pwd)/data:/app/data -v $(pwd)/artifacts:/app/artifacts \
#     conv-llm-finetune:gpu python src/sft/train_sft.py \
#       --model-name <a-larger-real-model> --use-qlora
FROM nvidia/cuda:12.4.1-runtime-ubuntu22.04

RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
    python3.11 python3-pip \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

WORKDIR /app

COPY requirements.txt .
# CUDA build of torch, matched to the base image's CUDA 12.4 -- swap the
# index URL if you change the base image's CUDA version.
RUN pip install --no-cache-dir torch --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu124 \
    && pip install --no-cache-dir -r requirements.txt \
    && pip install --no-cache-dir bitsandbytes

COPY scripts ./scripts
COPY src ./src

# No CMD: this image is meant to be run as `docker run ... python src/sft/train_sft.py ...`
# (or train_dpo.py / evaluate.py / merge_and_export.py), not as a long-running service --
# see Dockerfile (serving image) for that.
